# 2. LEARNING OBJECTIVES

This activity focuses on applying online-safety knowledge to different digital communication situations.

Students should be able to:

1. Examine different types of digital messages.
2. Identify suspicious features in senders, subjects, message bodies, requests and links.
3. Distinguish between safe, suspicious and uncertain messages.
4. Understand the consequences of unsafe online actions.
5. Choose appropriate actions when receiving suspicious messages.
6. Apply online-safety knowledge independently.

Preserve the original Year 5 English learning objectives and DSKP alignment.

Maintain the original 60-minute lesson structure.

This activity is an application and consolidation activity, not the final independent assessment.

